  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of Peace and Justice in the SADC Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to promote peace and justice for the victims of human rights violations in Mozambique, committed by State Actors, Non-State Actors, and multinational corporations. In addition, the project will contribute to ongoing efforts in addressing the crisis in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). Specifically the project will generate and share critical on-the-ground analysis of the DRC situation, providing valuable insights to our regional church partners. This timely and accurate analysis will be integral to their advocacy efforts, helping them push for peace, justice, and accountability both within the DRC and across the wider region. Broadly the project will contribute to a more effective regional response to these crises, fostering cooperation and shared solutions for peacebuilding and human rights protections.</narrative>
  </description>
